Open directories with O_SEARCH where O_PATH is missing (darwin).

Since 2.35.2 a path is read one directory at a time, and without O_PATH
each directory is opened O_RDONLY, which needs read permission on every
ancestor. A directory that grants search but not read breaks it:

  $ mkdir locked && echo '"hi"' > locked/f.nix && chmod 0311 locked
  $ nix eval --impure --expr 'import ./locked/f.nix'
  error: opening directory '.../locked': Permission denied

srt grants only metadata on the ancestors of what a session may read, so
inside srt every read by absolute path fails the same way, at /private or
/Users. O_SEARCH needs only search permission, which is all openat
beneath the directory requires.

Measured on 2.35.3 (2026-10-14): unit and functional tests pass (178 ok,
0 failed), and inside srt the patched client evaluates
darwinConfigurations.trex to the same derivation as the host. Not sent
upstream.

diff --git a/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc b/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc
index 55fa634..381b337 100644
--- a/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc
+++ b/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc
@@ -389,6 +389,9 @@ std::pair<Descriptor, std::shared_ptr<AutoCloseFD>> PosixDirectorySourceAccessor
 #  ifdef O_PATH
             /* As to not require read permissions on the directory. */
             O_PATH |
+#  elif defined(O_SEARCH)
+            /* Likewise: search permission is enough to resolve paths beneath it. */
+            O_SEARCH |
 #  else
             /* Sadly this will require read permissison for path resolution,
                but without O_PATH that's unavoidable. */
diff --git a/src/libutil/unix/file-system-at.cc b/src/libutil/unix/file-system-at.cc
index 18046ff..4e07db4 100644
--- a/src/libutil/unix/file-system-at.cc
+++ b/src/libutil/unix/file-system-at.cc
@@ -168,6 +168,8 @@ static AutoCloseFD openFileEnsureBeneathNoSymlinksIterative(
             O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC
 #ifdef __linux__
                 | O_PATH /* Linux-specific optimization. Files are open only for path resolution purposes. */
+#elif defined(O_SEARCH)
+                | O_SEARCH /* Needs search permission on the directory, not read permission. */
 #endif
 #ifdef __FreeBSD__
                 | O_RESOLVE_BENEATH /* Further guard against any possible SNAFUs. */
